{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:35932760 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:35932760 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"35932760","source":"MED","pmid":"35932760","doi":"10.1016/j.molcel.2022.07.003","title":"Endogenous ligand recognition and structural transition of a human PTH receptor.","authorString":"Kobayashi K, Kawakami K, Kusakizako T, Miyauchi H, Tomita A, Kobayashi K, Shihoya W, Yamashita K, Nishizawa T, Kato HE, Inoue A, Nureki O.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Kobayashi K","firstName":"Kazuhiro","lastName":"Kobayashi","initials":"K","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Graduate School of Science, the University of Tokyo, Bunkyo, Tokyo 113-0033, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Kawakami K","firstName":"Kouki","lastName":"Kawakami","initials":"K","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2507-8619"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Graduate School of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Tohoku University, Sendai, Miyagi 980-8578, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Kusakizako T","firstName":"Tsukasa","lastName":"Kusakizako","initials":"T","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6186-6647"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Graduate School of Science, the University of Tokyo, Bunkyo, Tokyo 113-0033, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Miyauchi H","firstName":"Hirotake","lastName":"Miyauchi","initials":"H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Graduate School of Science, the University of Tokyo, Bunkyo, Tokyo 113-0033, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Tomita A","firstName":"Atsuhiro","lastName":"Tomita","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3887-1429"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Graduate School of Science, the University of Tokyo, Bunkyo, Tokyo 113-0033, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Kobayashi K","firstName":"Kan","lastName":"Kobayashi","initials":"K","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Graduate School of Science, the University of Tokyo, Bunkyo, Tokyo 113-0033, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Shihoya W","firstName":"Wataru","lastName":"Shihoya","initials":"W","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Graduate School of Science, the University of Tokyo, Bunkyo, Tokyo 113-0033, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Yamashita K","firstName":"Keitaro","lastName":"Yamashita","initials":"K","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5442-7582"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Graduate School of Science, the University of Tokyo, Bunkyo, Tokyo 113-0033, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Nishizawa T","firstName":"Tomohiro","lastName":"Nishizawa","initials":"T","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Graduate School of Science, the University of Tokyo, Bunkyo, Tokyo 113-0033, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Kato HE","firstName":"Hideaki E","lastName":"Kato","initials":"HE","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1941-5535"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Graduate School of Science, the University of Tokyo, Bunkyo, Tokyo 113-0033, Japan; Komaba Institute for Science, the University of Tokyo, Meguro, Tokyo 153-8505, Japan; FOREST, Japan Science and Technology Agency, Kawaguchi, Saitama 332-0012, Japan. Electronic address: hekato@bio.c.u-tokyo.ac.jp."}]}},{"fullName":"Inoue A","firstName":"Asuka","lastName":"Inoue","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Graduate School of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Tohoku University, Sendai, Miyagi 980-8578, Japan. Electronic address: iaska@tohoku.ac.jp."}]}},{"fullName":"Nureki O","firstName":"Osamu","lastName":"Nureki","initials":"O","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Graduate School of Science, the University of Tokyo, Bunkyo, Tokyo 113-0033, Japan. Electronic address: nureki@bs.s.u-tokyo.ac.jp."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1941-5535"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2507-8619"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3366-3586"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5442-7582"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6186-6647"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3887-1429"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"18","volume":"82","journalIssueId":3424705,"dateOfPublication":"2022 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":2022,"printPublicationDate":"2022-09-01","journal":{"title":"Molecular cell","medlineAbbreviation":"Mol Cell","isoabbreviation":"Mol Cell","nlmid":"9802571","essn":"1097-4164","issn":"1097-2765"}},"pubYear":"2022","pageInfo":"3468-3483.e5","abstractText":"Endogenous parathyroid hormone (PTH) and PTH-related peptide (PTHrP) bind to the parathyroid hormone receptor 1 (PTH1R) and activate the stimulatory G-protein (Gs) signaling pathway. Intriguingly, the two ligands have distinct signaling and physiological properties: PTH evokes prolonged Gs activation, whereas PTHrP evokes transient Gs activation with reduced bone-resorption effects. The distinct molecular actions are ascribed to the differences in ligand recognition and dissociation kinetics. Here, we report cryoelectron microscopic structures of six forms of the human PTH1R-Gs complex in the presence of PTH or PTHrP at resolutions of 2.8 -4.1 Å. A comparison of the PTH-bound and PTHrP-bound structures reveals distinct ligand-receptor interactions underlying the ligand affinity and selectivity. Furthermore, five distinct PTH-bound structures, combined with computational analyses, provide insights into the unique and complex process of ligand dissociation from the receptor and shed light on the distinct durations of signaling induced by PTH and PTHrP.","affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Graduate School of Science, the University of Tokyo, Bunkyo, Tokyo 113-0033, Japan.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"grantId":"JPMJMS2023","agency":"Moonshot Research and Development Program","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"LEAP JP20gm0010004","agency":"Inamori Foundation","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R01 CA129325","agency":"NCI NIH HHS","acronym":"CA","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Daiichi Sankyo Foundation of Life Science","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Mochida Memorial Foundation for Medical and Pharmaceutical Research","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"19H03163","agency":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"JPMJFR215T","agency":"Fusion Oriented REsearch for disruptive Science and Technology","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Tokyo Biochemical Research Foundation","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"16H06294","agency":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"21H05113","agency":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"JPJSBP120213501","agency":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Japan Cabinet Office","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"20J21820","agency":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"JPJSBP120218801","agency":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"Nb35","agency":"National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"21H05142","agency":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"BINDS JP20am0101095","agency":"Inamori Foundation","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"19gm5910013","agency":"AMED","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"21H04791","agency":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Uehara Memorial Foundation","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Astellas Foundation for Research on Metabolic Disorders","orderIn":0},{"agency":"JST","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Kao Foundation for Arts and Sciences","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Takeda Science Foundation","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R01-GM129325","agency":"National Institutes of Health","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Parathyroid Hormone-Related Protein","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Parathyroid Hormone","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"PD","qualifierName":"pharmacology","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"GTP-Binding Protein alpha Subunits, Gs","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Receptor, Parathyroid Hormone, Type 1","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Ligands"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Inactivation","Dynamics","Activation","Cryoelectron microscopy","Gpcr","Class B Gpcr","Parathyroid Hormone Type 1 Receptor","Ligand Kinetics"]},"chemical